{
  "schema": "trial/1",
  "trial": "P-71",
  "question": "What does GitHub answer to each request of a push by the git data API, in the order `guards/push.py` permits them: the read of a commit (`GET /repos/{repo}/git/commits/{sha}`), of its tree whole (`GET /repos/{repo}/git/trees/{sha}?recursive=1`), of a blob it names (`GET /repos/{repo}/git/blobs/{sha}`) and of a work branch that is absent (`GET /repos/{repo}/git/ref/heads/{branch}`); the making of a blob (`POST /repos/{repo}/git/blobs`), of a tree upon the commit's that writes a file, writes an executable file and removes one (`POST /repos/{repo}/git/trees`), of a commit of it on one parent (`POST /repos/{repo}/git/commits`), and of the branch (`POST /repos/{repo}/git/refs`), each read back; a move of the branch to a child commit without force (`PATCH /repos/{repo}/git/refs/heads/{branch}`), read back; and what does it answer to the branch made again where it stands, and moved without force to a commit that is not a descendant of its head?",
  "pass": "Written before the run, in the design's row for P-71 at commit 789b740 of the Factory's repo, committed 2026-11-20T16:17:14Z, before the trial's first request (16:18:06Z): Each answer is the one `guards/push.py` assumes, so its `seen`, given the recorded exchanges in order with each status as text, takes every one and leaves the push landed, once where the branch is made and once where it is moved (issue 838): a read answers 200, a blob, a tree, a commit or a branch made 201, a move 200; a commit gives its `sha`, `tree.sha`, its one parent's `sha` and `message` as sent; a tree's listing gives its `sha`, `truncated` as the JSON false and each entry's `path`, `mode`, `type` and `sha`, a directory as `040000` of type `tree`, an executable file as `100755` and a symlink as `120000`, each of type `blob`; a blob gives its `sha`, `content` and `encoding` as `base64`; the absent branch answers 404; a branch made, moved or read gives `ref` as `refs/heads/` and the branch, and `object.sha` its commit; the tree made reads back as the commit's listing with exactly the changes in it; and the branch made again and the move that is not a fast-forward are each refused with a status that is no success, the branch left where it stood. Any other answer is recorded as the difference it is, and the trial fails. Asked as the Maintainer, through his `gh` login, as P-68 was: the answers' shape does not depend on who asks. This file holds push A, which makes the branch, and the branch made again; `trials/P-71.moved.json` holds push B, which moves it, and the two moves refused.",
  "repo": "combsmith/software-factory-canary",
  "ran_at": "2026-11-20T16:18:06Z",
